<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/>
  <title>Nicolás Medina Sánchez</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=EB+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400;1,500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

    :root {
      --text:  #1a1916;
      --muted: #6b6860;
      --faint: #c8c4bc;
      --bg:    #faf9f7;
    }

    body {
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: 'EB Garamond', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      max-width: 640px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 5rem 2rem 7rem;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      font-weight: 400;
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      line-height: 1.2;
      margin-bottom: 2.2rem;
    }

    .epigraph {
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      border-left: 1px solid var(--faint);
    }

    .epigraph p {
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .epigraph cite {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 0.4rem;
      font-style: normal;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      color: var(--faint);
    }

    .body-text {
      margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    }

    .body-text:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }

    section {
      margin-top: 3.2rem;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 400;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
    }

    .pub {
      margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
      padding-bottom: 1.4rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--faint);
    }

    .pub:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
      margin-bottom: 0;
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    .pub-title {
      display: block;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.55;
      margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
    }

    .pub-authors {
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-style: italic;
    }

    .pub-ref {
      display: block;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 0.15rem;
    }

    .talk {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 2.8rem 1fr;
      gap: 0 0.8rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .talk:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .talk-year {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      padding-top: 0.18rem;
    }

    .talk-body { line-height: 1.55; }

    .talk-where {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .talk-title {
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
    }

    .contact {
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 3.5rem;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--faint);
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>Nicolás Medina Sánchez</h1>

  <div class="epigraph">
    <p>Toute séparation est un lien.</p>
    <cite>Simone Weil, <em>La pesanteur et la grâce</em></cite>
  </div>

  <p class="body-text">
    I am a physicist and mathematician working on the operational and axiomatic
    reconstruction of physical theories. My research concerns the structural foundations
    of quantum theory, spacetime physics, statistical mechanics, and the quantum-to-classical
    transition, as well as chaos and nonlinear dynamics.
  </p>

  <p class="body-text">
    My approach draws on category theory, topos theory, categorical logic, differential geometry,
    topology, functional analysis, operator algebras, combinatorics, and probability theory.
    The underlying aim is to understand how spacetime, quantum phenomena, and statistical
    structures emerge from operationally meaningful principles and invariant relational data.
  </p>

  <p class="body-text">
    Philosophically, my work sits at the intersection of phenomenology, cybernetics,
    and propensity-based interpretations of probability. I take physical theory to be
    a structure of operations, constraints, and invariant relations rather than a
    representation of underlying substances.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Publications</h2>

    <div class="pub">
      <span class="pub-title">Reconstruction of Quantum Fields: CCR, CAR and Transfields</span>
      <span class="pub-authors">N. Medina Sánchez, B. Dakić</span>
      <span class="pub-ref">arXiv:2512.16775 (2025)</span>
    </div>

    <div class="pub">
      <span class="pub-title">The classical limit of quantum mechanics through coarse-grained measurements</span>
      <span class="pub-authors">F. Bibak, C. Cepollaro, N. Medina Sánchez, B. Dakić, Č. Brukner</span>
      <span class="pub-ref">arXiv:2503.15642 [quant-ph] (2025)</span>
    </div>

    <div class="pub">
      <span class="pub-title">Reconstruction of Quantum Particle Statistics: Bosons, Fermions, and Transtatistics</span>
      <span class="pub-authors">N. Medina Sánchez, B. Dakić</span>
      <span class="pub-ref">Quantum 8, 1473 (2024) · arXiv:2306.05919</span>
    </div>

    <div class="pub">
      <span class="pub-title">Punchets: nonlinear transport in Hamiltonian pump-ratchet hybrids</span>
      <span class="pub-authors">T. Dittrich, N. Medina Sánchez</span>
      <span class="pub-ref">J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 51, 055101 (2017) · arXiv:1708.05701</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
